      "writtenOn": "2023-04-05T16:50:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel like it\u0027s pretty valuable - it saves considerable CPU work and memory allocation, etc... In terms of not having the right codec, I think there\u0027s really two situations where we\u0027re deserializing:\n\n1) Client has code that runs on both ends. In this case, if they were able to load/use a particular format when they initially created the image and serialized it, then we can assume they still have support for it when they re-decode the picture?\n2) Client spits out an SKP and hands it to us for debugging purposes. In that case, I think we\u0027re fine -- our tools are going to include all the codecs, right?",
